I'v seen this behavior once with an old version of Nethack for ATARI.
The svave/restore code (even in 3.0j) assumes a fixed relation between 
data and codearea (it stores POINTERS to strings in the savefiles ((well,
OFFSETS is more correct))).
This is true for almost all UNIX derivates.
I presume AIX assignes each process a seperate dataarea with no fixed relation
to the textsegment (code). This would IMO explain this gibberish.

